    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0370" n="310" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg310"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Webb.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 238.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-11-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 17, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your dispatch of the 8th ultimo, without
                    number, has been received. The recent events in Paraguay to which it refers may
                    be regarded as painfully important. The letter<anchor n="*" xml:id="d197-f1"/>
                    of this department to the Secretary of the Navy, a copy of which is inclosed,
                    has been approved by the President, and may be accepted as our present
                    impression in regard to affairs in that quarter. Any further measures which may
                    be considered or adopted will depend upon future developments.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James Watson Webb,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d197-f1" n="*" xml:id="d197-f1-content">
                <p>For this inclosure see instructions to Mr. Washburn, No. 78, November 17,
                    1868.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
